@@ -782,10 +782,18 @@ refused instead. So is an index past the end of a log that holds records,
 which is what a changelog restarted after its last user was deregistered and
 the MDT remounted looks like; once the new log grows past the recorded index
 that can no longer be seen. Every MDT is checked before the search starts,
-so a purge that reaches a later MDT while an earlier one is being read is
-not caught. Nor is one record lost to a race in the MDT: records are written
