+.I FILE
+is not rewritten, so every later run is refused the same way until
+.I FILE
+is removed. Not caught: a purge that empties that log, until new records
+arrive; a purge on the MDT being read, which on a single-MDT filesystem is
+the only window there is. Nor is one record lost to a race in the MDT:
+records are written in parallel, so a run that reaches the end of a busy log
+can read record N+1 before N is complete, and the next run starts past N.
+Keep
 .I FILE
 outside the searched tree; the run writes it, so inside the tree it reports
 itself on every run. To accept the gap and go on, remove
diff --git a/Documentation/man3/llapi_find_since.3 b/Documentation/man3/llapi_find_since.3
